 output in a convenient way you can  do all kinds of manipulations but in a  safe way so when you do an invalid  operation you will receive an error and  you have also have type information that  prevents from  you from doing stuff that is not allowed  to do  and um yeah this so far this has been a  really great abstraction that made the  role of jupiter lab itself very easy to  use  very easy  um  much much simpler because the jupyter ui  only needs to listen to changes from the  jupiter notebook and render them in the  interface it doesn't have to deal with  the representation of the shared  notebook anymore  and  it is actually now fairly easy to build  your own custom youtuber ui  to build to render your own custom  uh representation of the notebook for  example maybe you want to use a  different editor all of that is now  easily possible  for extension authors this is great  because for the first time it is easy to  extract the content from a gypton  notebook and also observe in real time  when something changes you get easy to  use easy to understand events whenever a  cell is added or when content to a cell  was added when metadata was manipulated  this is not hidden information anymore  we expose this in a  great interface that is typed in  typescript  that allows you to well now build  features that you weren't able to do  before  and also  you can deal with all the collaborative  scenarios like for example  you have access to the awareness  information which includes for example  the number of users and which user are  currently online and where their cursor  location is  you can use this to render some  additional meta information on top of  your current  local user  user for example in order to provide a  help dialogue  and you can also  maybe provide  custom collaboration extensions that use  awareness information to provide  additional context that is important for  your specific  scenario  and yeah and if all of that is not  enough you can use yours f